                      (        forth.asm):04104         * The algorithm implemented here is similar to Donald's Knuth algorithm M,
                      (        forth.asm):04105         * as described in "The Art of Computer Programming", Volume II, 3rd edition,
                      (        forth.asm):04106         * section 4.3.1, pp 268. It is not as generic as algorithm M but fits our
                      (        forth.asm):04107         * particular purpose here: a 16x16 bit unsigned multiplication that yields
                      (        forth.asm):04108         * a 32 bit result. A simpler description of algorithm M can be found in
                      (        forth.asm):04109         * Henry S. Warren Junior's "Hacker's Delight", second edition, section 8-1,
                      (        forth.asm):04110         * pp 171. A C prototype implementation for a little endian host is provided
                      (        forth.asm):04111         * in SW/util/umstar.c.
                      (        forth.asm):04112         * In essence we reduce the problem to a 2 digit by 2 digit (expressed in
                      (        forth.asm):04113         * base 256) multiplication and use the 6809 MUL (A * B -> D) instruction.
